extends RefCounted
## The tawny owl, drawn by hand in the style of the animals redrawn from the user's references (thread
## «Нарисовать воробья, белку, ворону и утку», 2026-11-21; approved by the user). The project
## library's survivium-builds/animals/anim/wild4/ has the reviews; the frames are tools/art/animals/
## ow.py, written here by write_wild_art.py. tools/make_sprites.gd saves it as the owl
## bundle's picture (content/animals/owl/sprites/creatures/owl.png), the sheet Creatures draws from.
##
## Every state has at most four frames (the user's rule) for the south (as it comes at the camera),
## the north (as it goes away) and the west; the east is the west mirrored, as the game draws it.
## No frames of hurt (the user's pick: the game flashes a struck animal red on its own frame) and one
## of death, which stays till its carcass is taken.
##
## A frame is rows of letters of INK ("." empty), the outline drawn as letters too. The frames of a
## view share one canvas, so the body does not jump between states; its last row is the ground (in
## the air the game lifts the whole sprite).

## The colours of the letters.
